{"timestamp": 1779383612.087734, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I reported Eve\u2019s body in Weapons. I came storage -> navigation -> security -> weapons. I saw Charlie enter navigation from security around tick 10, then I continued through security up to weapons and found Eve dead there. Meeting shows Alice is dead too, apparently her body was in Electrical. I didn\u2019t see Diana or Frank this round. Charlie was the only person I crossed paths with, and security is between Electrical and Weapons, so that timing/location is worth noting."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383621.520212, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I was in Weapons around tick 4-5 with Charlie and Eve \u2014 both alive when I left. I went back through security and ended up in Electrical at tick 12, where I saw Alice come in from cafeteria. I didn't see her die \u2014 I must've just missed it, or she was killed right after I moved. \n\nSo to lay it out: my route was navigation -> security -> weapons -> security -> electrical. Eve was alive in Weapons when I left. Charlie was with us in Weapons at tick 4, then I saw him in Security at tick 7 heading\u2026 somewhere. Bob, you said you saw Charlie enter navigation from security around tick 10 \u2014 that lines up with Charlie's direction of travel.\n\nBut here's what bothers me: someone killed Eve in Weapons AFTER I left, and someone killed Alice in Electrical right around when I was there. Two kills, opposite sides of the map. Either there are two killers, or one killer moved fast. Bob, you ended up in Weapons and found Eve \u2014 you came from security too. Where exactly were you between ticks 5 and 10? And Frank \u2014 I haven't seen Frank at all this round, which is suspicious to me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383644.765873, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was Weapons \u2192 Security \u2192 Navigation. I saw Eve alive in Weapons ticks 2, 3, and 4, and Diana was also there at tick 4. Then I moved through Security \u2014 Diana saw me there around tick 7 \u2014 and I went to Navigation. At tick 10, I saw Bob leaving Navigation toward Security, which matches him saying he went Navigation \u2192 Security \u2192 Weapons.\n\nSo I definitely was not near Electrical for Alice. For Eve, yes, I was in Weapons early, but Eve was alive when I left and Diana can confirm I moved out through Security.\n\nWhat worries me most is the Alice kill: Diana says she was in Electrical at tick 12 and Alice came in from Cafeteria, then Alice ends up dead. That is very close timing. I\u2019m not hard accusing yet, but Diana is the closest confirmed person to one body. Frank being completely unseen is also a problem, so I really need to hear Frank\u2019s route. Bob\u2019s story mostly lines up with what I saw."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383666.779874, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I was not hiding \u2014 my route was Electrical \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Storage, and I didn\u2019t encounter anyone the whole round. I also did not see Alice in Electrical at all, so I must have left before she came in from Cafeteria like Diana described.\n\nFrom what everyone said, Bob and Charlie\u2019s stories line up with each other around Navigation/Security at tick 10. Charlie was seen leaving Weapons earlier and then in Security/Navigation, so he\u2019s less likely for Alice. Bob found Eve, so self-report is possible, but his route is corroborated by Charlie.\n\nThe biggest issue to me is Diana. She was in Weapons with Eve earlier, then later she says she was in Electrical right when Alice came in, and Alice is now dead there. That\u2019s close to both bodies. I think Diana has the strongest opportunity based on the info we have."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383687.3657842, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "To answer Diana: between ticks 5 and 10 I was moving Storage \u2192 Navigation, then at tick 10 I saw Charlie come into Navigation from Security. After that I went Navigation \u2192 Security \u2192 Weapons and immediately found Eve\u2019s body.\n\nCharlie\u2019s account matches mine pretty well, and Diana also saw Charlie leave Weapons earlier, so I\u2019m less suspicious of Charlie right now. Frank is still totally unconfirmed, but based on everyone\u2019s routes, Diana was close to both bodies: Weapons with Eve early, then Electrical right when Alice was there and ended up dead. That\u2019s the strongest lead I see so far."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383699.754592, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Look, I get why I'm getting heat \u2014 I was near both rooms. But let's actually think about timing, not just proximity.\n\nEve was alive in Weapons at tick 5 when I left. Charlie confirms he was in Weapons through tick 4 and Eve was alive then too. For me to have killed Eve, I'd have had to do it at tick 4 or 5 \u2014 but Charlie was right there with us. Charlie, did you see Eve get killed? No. Because she was alive. So someone came into Weapons AFTER both Charlie and I left and killed her. That's not me \u2014 I was already moving back through Security toward Electrical.\n\nFor Alice \u2014 I entered Electrical at tick 12 and Alice came in from Cafeteria at tick 12. If I killed her, the body would've been found basically the moment I left. And here's the thing: I didn't report it. Why would a killer leave a fresh body in a room they were just seen entering, and then NOT report? That's the worst possible play.\n\nNow, Frank \u2014 you say your route was Electrical \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Storage and you saw nobody the entire round. Electrical is exactly where Alice died. You were there BEFORE me. You could have killed Alice and left, and then I walked in right after. The timing fits you better than me, honestly. \"I left before she came in\" is convenient when there's no one to corroborate.\n\nBob's route is corroborated by Charlie. Charlie's route is corroborated by me and Bob. I'm corroborated by Charlie in Weapons and I witnessed Alice entering Electrical alive. Frank is corroborated by literally no one.\n\nMy vote is going on Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383741.630177, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I still think the key is: with only one Duck, whoever did this probably needs a route that can explain both bodies, not just one.\n\nBob and I confirm each other at Navigation/Security around tick 10, and Bob finding Eve after that makes sense timing-wise. Frank is unconfirmed, which is bad, but his claimed route doesn\u2019t really explain Eve unless he\u2019s lying about basically everything.\n\nDiana, you\u2019re right that I didn\u2019t see you kill Eve \u2014 Eve was alive when I last saw her. But you were the last confirmed person with Eve in Weapons, then I saw you in Security at tick 7, and then you place yourself in Electrical right when Alice was there and later dead. That route can physically connect both deaths.\n\nFrank is suspicious for being unseen, but Diana has the strongest confirmed opportunity on both bodies. I\u2019m leaning Diana here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383763.855773, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I\u2019m going to be clear: I\u2019m unconfirmed, yes, but Diana\u2019s version actually makes me less likely for Alice, not more. She says Alice entered Electrical alive at tick 12. I was already gone on my route Electrical \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Storage and never saw Alice at all. If Alice was alive when Diana saw her, then I did not kill Alice before leaving.\n\nFor Eve, Bob and Charlie line up with each other, and Charlie saw Diana leave Weapons after being there with Eve. Diana\u2019s route is the one that connects Weapons early and Electrical late. She was near Eve, then near Alice right when Alice ended up dead.\n\nBeing unseen is fair to question, but Diana has the actual confirmed opportunity on both bodies. I think we should vote Diana."}}
